  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The cell potential for the given cell at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Pt</mi><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>bar</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8214;</mo><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mi>Cu</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi></math> of the acidic solution is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>, whereas the concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is _________.</p><p>(Given:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Cu</mi></mrow><mi>&#920;</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>34</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn><mi>RT</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>06</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>)</p>"
  },
